  "details": "When doing local build and testing with a video player, there is an Error log output:\n\n`Error      -  You are playing an untrusted URL (Domain: -snip-) in a local world. If this URL is needed for the world to work, the domain needs to be added to the world's Video Player Allowed Domains list on the website.`\n\nThis is might confuse or worry users who don't fully understand about what or why they are being errored.\n\nI think the message itself is fine personally, but I believe the log level should be a normal LOG statement, or at most, a WARNING.\n\nWhen users see ERROR, they might think something is critically wrong. Since local build and test has no world ID enabled, it should not portray such information as a failure/error.",
